{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1790345200000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-final.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '1,340p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-25 14:52:46 GMT\n     2\tCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 21:52:46 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n     3\t\n     4\tConsensus confirmed. Codex granted sign-off on the design, with one binding ruling and three non-blocking corrections. I verified each against the tree and accept all four. The consolidated design follows; it stands alone.\n     5\t\n     6\t## Rulings on codex's final points\n     7\t\n     8\t**Fold Change A into B: ACCEPT.** UCF section 7.3.3 puts resolver precedence inside the stamped contract and says a changed resolution order is a new revision (UCF 262 to 274). A resolver that skips env and store for one name is a precedence change, so it cannot ship as an erratum. Codex's second reason also holds: while `yin/def` stays a registry entry, `empty-state` accepts a composition-supplied registry (vm.cljc:1623), so registry-only lookup still does not fix its meaning. Two commits.\n     9\t\n    10\t**P2, store-write lint: ACCEPT.** My \"no assoc into the store outside the engine\" rule was wrong as a proof. The tree has eleven store-write sites: the dispatcher (engine.cljc:512), the ready-queue merge (engine.cljc:425), four direct instructions (walker 419 to 438, semantic.cljc:303, stack.cljc:486, register.cljc:486), two constructor merges (stack.cljc:149, register.cljc:164), dao.await (await.cljc:222), the REPL's history keys (repl.cljc:600), and the handoff demo (continuation_handoff.cljc:208). The rule becomes an exact allowlist audit, stated in the design below.\n    11\t\n    12\t**P2, producers: ACCEPT.** The walker's own `vm/eval` builds datoms from a map AST and loads them (ast_walker.cljc:765 to 775), and the expander's transformer runner builds a row set and loads it (macro.cljc:723 to 732). Both are trusted fresh-code producers and must pass the current contract explicitly.\n    13\t\n    14\t**P2, raw control: ACCEPT.** A walker stepped through `cesk-transition` with supplied control has no load event (ast_walker.cljc:688), so its refusals are transition-time by definition, including a reserved store-get or store-update key.\n    15\t\n    16\t**Correction to the proof wording: ACCEPT.** `unsatisfied-names` takes a supplied callback (ucf.cljc:387 to 395); it is a static check, not a resolver caller. The proof covers every executing VM variable lookup.\n    17\t\n    18\t**Walker datom loader gap: ACCEPT.** `datoms->ast` reconstructs without whole-tree validation (vm.cljc:646), so the walker's datom loader is a second unvalidated admission path beside the stack loader.\n    19\t\n    20\tNothing material remains in dispute between codex and me.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Final design: yin/def is syntax, never a name\n    23\t\n    24\t**Diagnosis.** The front end already treats `def` as a special form, but lowers it to an ordinary call of a primitive named `yin/def`, and every engine resolves that name through env, then store, then primitives, so a parameter, a store write, a computed key, or a passed-around primitive value can change what a later definition does. The M2 linker recognizes definitions by that syntactic shape, so the shadowing makes its discharge of use-before-definition obligations unsound, and four gate rounds each found a new route.\n    25\t\n    26\t**Rule R, by syntactic role.**\n    27\t\n    28\t- A `:variable` naming `yin/def` is legal only as the operator of a two-operand application whose first operand is a literal symbol other than `yin/def`. Every other variable occurrence is refused.\n    29\t- `yin/def` is not a binder: not a lambda parameter, not a supplied env key.\n    30\t- `yin/def` is not a store key: not in a store-put, store-get, or store-update node or instruction, not in a store-put effect, not in a supplied or restored store.\n    31\t- `yin/def` is not a definition key or a macro name.\n    32\t- A literal whose value is the symbol `yin/def` is ordinary data and is allowed anywhere.\n    33\t- `yin/def` is not a primitive and has no profile. A registry containing it is refused.\n    34\t- Redefining any other name stays allowed.\n    35\t\n    36\t**Scope.** `yin/def` only. `require` is dynamic and not statically interpreted, so shadowing it is not a soundness hole. The reserved set is a one-entry contract table.\n    37\t\n    38\t**The two-function proof.** Every executing VM variable lookup goes through `engine/resolve-var`: the walker at two sites, the semantic, stack, and register VMs at one each. If that function refuses `yin/def` before it consults env or store, and the definition transition in each engine never resolves its operator, then no loader, supplied env, store entry, scheduler merge, or restored snapshot can redirect a definition. Completeness condition: **a program is sound with respect to definitions when every executing variable lookup passes through `resolve-var` and every valid definition form writes its literal key without resolving its operator.** That condition holds by inspection of the four engines today for the first half and by the transition change for the second. Load-time validation and the store-key invariant are additional requirements, not the proof.\n    39\t\n    40\t**Load-time refusal, still required.** Whole-tree, occurrence-aware checks in `validate-rows` and `semantic-bytecode->ast`; reserved-operand and `:define` rules in `code/well-formed?` and `code/well-formed-vector?`; the stack and register image validators; the walker's datom loader and the stack loader start validating; the four linker format records wrap these. Raw control stepped directly refuses at transition time.\n    41\t\n    42\t**Store-key invariant, separate and audited.** Program writes, meaning the dispatcher and the four direct instructions, route through one `engine/store-put` that refuses the reserved key. The remaining sites are state construction and are an exact allowlist: the ready-queue merge (asserted to carry only engine-minted keyword keys), the two constructor merges (checked), dao.await (minted keyword keys, checked), the REPL history keys (fixed symbols, not reserved), the handoff demo, and the M4 module-store lower. The gate greps for store writes and fails on any site outside the allowlist.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Expander.** Context construction and batch expansion refuse a store binding the name; harvest refuses the key. The transformer runner is a walker and inherits the transition checks.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Contract stamps.** AST and semantic move to \"v3\", stack to \"b2\", register to \"r2\". Every persistent-code admission requires a stamp and compares it: the linker fetch refuses an omitted contract as `:invalid-request`; manifests and derivation records carry the new names; the walker's datom and row loaders, the semantic datom and vector loaders, and the stack and register loaders take a required contract and refuse `:contract-missing` or `:contract-mismatch` before validation. An old-stamped image with no definition fails by stamp, not by grammar. Fresh code is a separate, explicit path: yang, the linearizers, the expander, `vm/eval`, and the transformer runner supply the current constant from `yin.vm` themselves. Nothing ever assigns a stamp to externally supplied datoms or rows.\n    47\t\n    48\t**Commit one, atomic Rule R.** Scope: resolver refusal before env; definition transition in all four engines; `:define` opcodes (semantic on the value register, stack popping the value, register with destination and source); `yin/def` removed from the registry and profiles; `engine/store-put` and the allowlist audit; every validator and loader above; required stamps and producer stamping; `free-names` excluding the definition operator; expander refusals; constructor checks; the docs below. Gate: JVM, Node, and Dart lanes, the parity harness, kondo, cljstyle, the store-write audit. Tests per host: each reserved role refused at load on every loader, including the semantic datom loader and the walker datom loader; the same refused at transition on raw control, including store-get and store-update keys; a supplied store, env, or registry binding the name refused at construction; a seeded macro named `yin/def` refused at context construction; identical stores across all four backends for the same definition programs; a lowered image with the old call shape refused; an old-stamped image with no definition refused by stamp; an unstamped load refused; a `vm/eval` and a transformer run succeed under the current stamp; a parked read inside a definition's value operand resumes in-process and writes the store on the walker and semantic VM; redefining `x` twice reads the second value.\n    49\t\n    50\t**Commit two, M2.** Scope: format records take the new contract names and the fetch requires one; the round 3 and 4 shadow filters and the `:yin-def?` bookkeeping are deleted; constant-key recognition, invocation position, dominance, and the earlier bound fixes stay; the vector definitions scanner reads `:define`; obligations exclude the operator; the rebinding, direct store-put, computed-key, and alias fixtures refuse `:reserved-name`; a definition whose value is the quoted symbol links. Gate: the existing M2 gate, run once.\n    51\t\n    52\t**M4 bucket, explicit obligations not passing today.** UCF frame encoding of a define frame; stamp comparison at continuation lowering; module-store snapshot lowering through `engine/store-put`; the lift and lower round trip.\n    53\t\n    54\t**Docs.** UCF 7.3.3, 7.5.2, 7.6.1, 7.11 and the revisions log; linker.md 4.1, 4.2, section 5 records, 6.3, 6.4, 8.1, section 11; yin.vm.semantic.md 2.4, 2.6, 4.2; code-as-tuples 4.5, 7.5, and the \"free at that site\" clause near line 1831; yin.vm.macro.md 2.2, 4.1, 4.2; debruijn.stack.md loader and instruction sections; debruijn.register.md 4.4; yin.vm.engine.md; yin-repl-design; datom.world.md, one line naming the store-write audit.\n    55\t\n    56\t**Defects versus deferred.** Defects, pre-existing: the stack loader admits without validation; the walker datom loader admits without whole-tree validation; no loader compares a contract; the M2 fetch admits an omitted contract. Deferred, admissible: store-update discovery, advisory export verification, host effects with computed keys under incomplete discovery, and the M4 bucket.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Residual risks.** A foreign engine that claims the new contract but resolves names outside the rule is caught only by the conformance corpus, not by construction. The producer-stamps rule depends on discipline in trusted code; the gate tests it but cannot prove it for future producers. Bumping four contracts invalidates every stored image and manifest; this repo has none deployed.\n    59\t\n    60\t**Owner decisions still open.**\n    61\t\n    62\t1. Whether `require` joins the reserved set now or waits until it gains static discovery. The design says wait.\n    63\t2. Whether the four contract bumps may invalidate every existing stored image and manifest without a migration path. The design assumes yes, per the no-backward-compatibility rule.\n    64\t3. Whether M2 stays uncommitted until commit one lands, which is what the two-commit order requires.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1790345800000-vm-engineer-yin-def-rule-r-commit-one.claude-opus-5-5.report.md | sed -n '1,340p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-25 15:56:19 GMT\n     2\tCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 22:56:19 +07\n     3\tCoding-Agent: claude\n     4\tSession-ID: 078d0a96-daf0-4cef-b994-076601d800d6\n     5\t\n     6\t# Report: Rule R, commit one (yin/def is syntax, never a name)\n     7\t\n     8\tRole: VM Runtime Engineer. Worktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-rule-r\n     9\t(branch ucf-rule-r, base 96657a4f). Nothing was staged or committed. All\n    10\tchanges are in the working tree: 60 tracked files changed, 1498 lines added\n    11\tand 468 removed, plus 2 new test files.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Lane counts\n    14\t\n    15\t| Lane | Baseline (96657a4f) | Final |\n    16\t|---|---|---|\n    17\t| JVM `clojure -M:test` | 2027 tests, 180638 assertions, 0 fail, 0 error | 2045 tests, 180913 assertions, 0 fail, 0 error |\n    18\t| Node `compile slice-peer test` | 1943 tests, 47718 assertions, 0 fail | 1960 tests, 47956 assertions, 0 fail |\n    19\t| Dart `bb test:cljd` (fresh cljd-out) | 1905 passed | 1922 passed |\n    20\t\n    21\tThe lanes ran one at a time under mise. The Node output shows \"Testing\n    22\tyin.vm.rule-r-test\", and the Dart output lists its tests. kondo on the\n    23\tchanged files reports 0 errors. Its 7 warnings all exist at base: I linted\n    24\tthe HEAD copies to confirm. `cljstyle check` passes on every changed file.\n    25\tEvery added or edited line in source and tests is ASCII and at most 80\n    26\tcolumns. The docs have one exception, noted below.\n    27\t\n    28\tEnvironment note: the Node baseline first failed with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`\n    29\tbecause the new worktree had no node_modules. I ran `npm ci` in the\n    30\tworktree. node_modules is gitignored.\n    31\t\n    32\t## What was implemented\n    33\t\n    34\tEverything below follows the design's \"Commit one\" paragraph.\n    35\t\n    36\t- **Resolver.** `engine/resolve-var` refuses a reserved name before it looks\n    37\t  at env or store: `{:rule :reserved-name :role :variable}`. The reserved\n    38\t  set is only `yin/def` (`vm/reserved-names`). `require` is unchanged and\n    39\t  still an ordinary primitive.\n    40\t- **Definition transition, all four engines.** No engine resolves the\n    41\t  operator.\n    42\t  - Walker: only the value operand is evaluated, under a pure-data\n    43\t    continuation `{:type :eval-define :name k}`, then the store is written.\n    44\t    The unused hot loop hands definitions to that same path.\n    45\t  - Semantic VM: `[:define name]`, opcode 24, writes the value register.\n    46\t  - Stack VM: `[:define name]` pops the value, writes it, and pushes it back\n    47\t    as the expression's value.\n    48\t  - Register VM: `[:define rd name rs]`.\n    49\t- **Lowerers and lifts.**\n    50\t  - The named datom lane and row lane emit the value, then `:define`.\n    51\t  - The de Bruijn resolver, `lower-stack` and `lower-register` do the same.\n    52\t  - The stack lift passes `:define` through. The register lift parses it.\n    53\t  - UCF `transitions` gets `:define :step`.\n    54\t  - The footprint table is keyed by the current contract and has a\n    55\t    `:define #{}` row.\n    56\t- **`yin/def` is removed** from `vm/primitives` and its profiles.\n    57\t  `empty-state` refuses a registry or profile table that binds it.\n    58\t- **`engine/store-put`** (with `check-store-key!`) refuses the reserved key.\n    59\t  These write through it:\n    60\t  - the `:vm/store-put` dispatcher;\n    61\t  - the direct store instructions in the four engines, including walker\n    62\t    `:vm/store-update`;\n    63\t  - all four definition transitions.\n    64\t\n    65\t  `resume-from-run-queue` refuses a store-update key that is not a keyword\n    66\t  (`:store-update-key`). dao.await makes the same check.\n    67\t- **Load-time validators.**\n    68\t  - `validate-rows`: new last rule `:reserved-name`. It is occurrence-aware:\n    69\t    a shared `[:variable yin/def]` row is judged at every parent slot and at\n    70\t    the root.\n    71\t  - `code/well-formed?`: batch rule 8, `:reserved-name`.\n    72\t  - `code/well-formed-vector?`: vector rule 9, `:reserved-name`.\n    73\t  - `debruijn-code/image-defect`: `reserved-defect`, run before the scope\n    74\t    check.\n    75\t  - Register validator: structural `reserved-rule`.\n    76\t- **Loaders.** The walker datom loader now validates the whole tree\n    77\t  (`vm/ast-reserved-defect`). The stack loader now validates\n    78\t  (`image-defect`).\n    79\t- **Transition-time refusal on raw walker control** covers: a reserved\n    80\t  variable, a lambda binding it, a store-get, store-put or store-update key\n    81\t  naming it, a malformed definition, and a raw `:eval-define` with the\n    82\t  reserved key.\n    83\t- **Contract stamps.** Defined in `yin.vm`: `ast-contract` \"v3\",\n    84\t  `semantic-contract` \"v3\", `stack-contract` \"b2\", `register-contract`\n    85\t  \"r2\", and `check-contract!`, which refuses with `:contract-missing` or\n    86\t  `:contract-mismatch` before validation. The UCF `contract-stamp` and the\n    87\t  ledger lowering profile use \"v3\".\n    88\t  - `debruijn-code/lowering-contract-version` goes to 2, and\n    89\t    `debruijn-register-code/contract-version` goes to 4. That moves every H,\n    90\t    R and descriptor hash.\n    91\t  - Loaders that now require a contract:\n    92\t    - walker `vm-load-program [vm datoms contract]`;\n    93\t    - walker `vm-load-rows [vm bc contract]`;\n    94\t    - semantic `vm-load-program [vm datoms contract]`;\n    95\t    - semantic `load-vector [vm v contract]` and `[vm v contract opts]`;\n    96\t    - stack and register `load-image [vm segment contract]`;\n    97\t    - stack and register `create-vm`, with `:contract` in opts, required\n    98\t      when the segment is non-empty.\n    99\t  - Fresh-code producers that pass the constant themselves:\n   100\t    - `vm/eval`;\n   101\t    - `linearize/ast-loader` and `rows-loader`;\n   102\t    - the REPL program loaders (expander output);\n   103\t    - the transformer runner (`bounded-row-evaluator`);\n   104\t    - the cljs and cljd demos.\n   105\t\n   106\t    The handoff demo ships its stamp inside its registers datom and never\n   107\t    assigns one to a received batch.\n   108\t- **Expander.** `make-ctx` refuses a seeded store that binds `yin/def` (a\n   109\t  macro named `yin/def`). `expand-batch` refuses a ctx store that binds it,\n   110\t  by throwing. `harvest` refuses it as a definition key.\n   111\t- **Constructor checks.**\n   112\t  - Walker and semantic refuse an `:env` that binds the name.\n   113\t  - Stack and register refuse a `:free-env` or `:store` that binds it.\n   114\t  - All four refuse a `:primitives` registry that binds it, through\n   115\t    `empty-state`.\n   116\t- **`free-names`** never returns the definition operator.\n   117\t- **Docs.** I delegated the doc edits to a subagent, gave it the design and\n   118\t  these facts, and reviewed the result. The docs are the ones the design\n   119\t  lists:\n   120\t  - UCF S7.3.3, S7.5.2, S7.6.1 and S7.11, plus a header revision entry (r4).\n   121\t    The UCF has no separate revisions log.\n   122\t  - linker.md 4.1, 4.2, section 5, 6.3, 6.4, 8.1 and section 11. The\n   123\t    commit-two fetch requirement is only noted as landing with the M2\n   124\t    format records.\n   125\t  - yin.vm.semantic.md 2.4, 2.6 and 4.2.\n   126\t  - code-as-tuples 4.5, 7.4, 7.5, 7.7.1 and 7.7.2, plus the \"free at that\n   127\t    site\" clause.\n   128\t  - yin.vm.macro.md 2.2, 4.1 and 4.2.\n   129\t  - debruijn.stack.md: loader and instruction sections.\n   130\t  - debruijn.register.md 4.4.\n   131\t  - yin.vm.engine.md: new section 1.1.\n   132\t  - yin-repl-design.md.\n   133\t  - datom.world.md: one line naming the store-write audit.\n   134\t\n   135\t## Files changed\n   136\t\n   137\t- **Source (23 files).** All under src/cljc/ unless noted:\n   138\t  - `yin/vm.cljc`\n   139\t  - `yin/vm/`: `engine.cljc`, `ast_walker.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`,\n   140\t    `code.cljc`, `ucf.cljc`, `linearize.cljc`, `debruijn_code.cljc`,\n   141\t    `debruijn_resolve.cljc`, `debruijn_linearize.cljc`,\n   142\t    `debruijn_register_code.cljc`, `debruijn_register_compile.cljc`,\n   143\t    `macro.cljc`, `ledger.cljc`, `completion.cljc`\n   144\t  - `yin/vm/debruijn/`: `stack.cljc`, `register.cljc`\n   145\t  - `yin/repl.cljc`\n   146\t  - `dao/await.cljc`\n   147\t  - `datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc`\n   148\t  - `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/`: `compilation_pipeline.cljs`,\n   149\t    `continuation_stream.cljs`\n   150\t  - `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd`\n   151\t- **Tests (27 files).**\n   152\t  - New: `test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc` and\n   153\t    `test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`.\n   154\t  - Updated: 25 files, for three reasons:\n   155\t    - loader call sites now pass stamps;\n   156\t    - fixtures that relied on `yin/def` as a primitive now use `:define` or\n   157\t      a `rec` primitive around a definition;\n   158\t    - golden H, R and descriptor hashes and golden bytes changed. The bytes\n   159\t      moved because `:define` joins the sorted mnemonic tag table.\n   160\t\n   161\t    Other updates in those 25 files:\n   162\t    - the R0 frozen register contract version is now 4;\n   163\t    - the corpus gained definitions and the reserved literal;\n   164\t    - `rows-loader` and `ast-loader` adapters now take 3 arguments;\n   165\t    - the stack loader now refuses an undefined opcode at load time\n   166\t      (`unknown-opcode-test`);\n   167\t    - the completion test asserts that `yin/def` is not a primitive\n   168\t      requirement.\n   169\t- **Docs (10 files):** the ones listed above.\n   170\t\n   171\t## Tests added\n   172\t\n   173\t`rule_r_test.cljc` runs on all three hosts: 17 tests, 178 assertions on the\n   174\tJVM.\n   175\t\n   176\t1. The resolver refuses the name before env and store. `require` stays\n   177\t   shadowable.\n   178\t2. There is no `yin/def` primitive or profile.\n   179\t3. All four backends write the same stores for five definition programs:\n   180\t   - define then read;\n   181\t   - redefine `x` twice, which reads the second value;\n   182\t   - a definition's own value;\n   183\t   - a stored closure called by name;\n   184\t   - the reserved symbol as a literal value, which is data.\n   185\t4. An env cannot redirect a definition.\n   186\t5. A read parked inside a definition's value operand resumes in-process and\n   187\t   writes the store, on the walker and on the semantic VM.\n   188\t6. Each reserved role is refused on the walker datom loader, the walker row\n   189\t   loader, `lower-ast` and the de Bruijn resolver. The roles are: variable,\n   190\t   operand, wrong arity, non-literal key, definition key, binder,\n   191\t   store-get key and store-put key.\n   192\t7. A shared row is judged at every occurrence.\n   193\t8. The semantic vector loader and datom loader refuse reserved operands,\n   194\t   including a lowered image in the old call shape.\n   195\t9. The stack loader (`create-vm` and `load-image`) refuses reserved\n   196\t   operands, including the old call shape.\n   197\t10. The register loader refuses reserved operands, including the old call\n   198\t    shape.\n   199\t11. Raw walker control is refused at transition time for each role,\n   200\t    including store-get, store-put and store-update keys and a raw\n   201\t    `:eval-define`.\n   202\t12. `engine/store-put` and the `:vm/store-put` effect refuse the key.\n   203\t13. A ready entry may carry only minted keyword keys.\n   204\t14. Construction refuses an env, store or registry that binds the name, on\n   205\t    all four VMs.\n   206\t15. The expander refuses the name in `make-ctx` (a seeded macro), in an\n   207\t    `expand-batch` ctx store, and as a harvested definition key. A\n   208\t    transformer run succeeds under the current stamp.\n   209\t16. On all six loaders, an unstamped load is refused (`:contract-missing`)\n   210\t    and an old-stamped image with no definition is refused by stamp\n   211\t    (`:contract-mismatch`). `vm/eval` succeeds.\n   212\t17. `free-names` excludes the definition operator.\n   213\t\n   214\t`store_write_audit_test.clj` is JVM-only because it reads source files. It\n   215\tis the exact-allowlist audit described in the next section.\n   216\t\n   217\t## Store-write allowlist (exact trimmed lines, by file)\n   218\t\n   219\t- **engine.cljc**\n   220\t  - `store-put`'s own `(assoc store key val)`.\n   221\t  - The dispatcher's `:store (store-put (:store state)`.\n   222\t  - Engine-minted keys:\n   223\t    - the stream id in `handle-make`;\n   224\t    - the cursor id in `handle-cursor`;\n   225\t    - the cursor advance in `handle-next`;\n   226\t    - the cursor advance in the waitset resolver `:advance`.\n   227\t  - The ready-queue merge, which asserts keyword keys.\n   228\t- **ast_walker.cljc**: the definition transition, and `:vm/store-put` and\n   229\t  `:vm/store-update`. All go through `engine/store-put`.\n   230\t- **semantic.cljc**: opcode 11 (`store-put`) and opcode 24 (`define`),\n   231\t  through `engine/store-put`.\n   232\t- **debruijn/stack.cljc**:\n   233\t  - the constructor merge (checked);\n   234\t  - `:store-put` and `:define`, through `engine/store-put`.\n   235\t- **debruijn/register.cljc**:\n   236\t  - the constructor merge (checked);\n   237\t  - `:store-put` and `:define`, through `engine/store-put`.\n   238\t- **dao/await.cljc**: the `store-updates` merge (keyword keys, checked).\n   239\t- **yin/repl.cljc**: the history keys `*1`, `*2` and `*3`.\n   240\t- **datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc**: the shipped `defs` merge\n   241\t  (checked).\n   242\t- **src/clj/yin/demo.clj**: a JVM demo moves one VM's whole store to\n   243\t  another.\n   244\t- **yin/vm/macro.cljc**: the expander's macro store. That is two lines in\n   245\t  harvest, which refuses the key, and two in post-harvest, which installs\n   246\t  only harvested names.\n   247\t\n   248\t## Deviations and findings\n   249\t\n   250\t1. **The design's store-write count is short.** The design lists eleven\n   251\t   sites. It misses these engine-internal writes of engine-minted keys:\n   252\t   - `handle-make`, which writes the stream id;\n   253\t   - `handle-cursor`, which writes the cursor id;\n   254\t   - `handle-next`, which advances the cursor;\n   255\t   - the waitset resolver `:advance`.\n   256\t\n   257\t   It also misses the JVM demo store transfer in `src/clj/yin/demo.clj`. I\n   258\t   put all of these on the allowlist with their reasons. None of them can\n   259\t   carry a program-chosen key.\n   260\t2. **Loader contract shape.** The design says \"take a required contract\". I\n   261\t   made it a required positional argument (`opts :contract` for the de\n   262\t   Bruijn `create-vm`).\n   263\t\n   264\t   The consequence: an observer composition whose medium carries fresh\n   265\t   producer output has to pass the constant itself. `test_utils/run-session`\n   266\t   does this, and so does one semantic observer test. This is my reading of\n   267\t   \"producers supply the current constant\". A composition over an external\n   268\t   medium has no stamp to pass unless the medium carries one. If the owner\n   269\t   wants stamps to travel inside batches instead, that is a design change.\n   270\t3. **Stack VM `:define`.** It pops the value and pushes it back as the\n   271\t   expression's value, so the net stack effect is 0. This keeps a\n   272\t   definition an expression, as the old `yin/def` call was, and it keeps\n   273\t   the stack lift equal to the named vector (`value, [:define name]`).\n   274\t4. **Contract names are new code.** \"b1\" and \"r1\" existed only in\n   275\t   linker.md. Before this change the code carried only integer versions for\n   276\t   stack and register. I added the string constants to `yin.vm` and bumped\n   277\t   the integer versions (stack lowering 1 to 2, register 3 to 4) so that H\n   278\t   and R move with the contract.\n   279\t5. **Footprint.** `:define` contributes `#{}`, the same as `:store-put`. As\n   280\t   a result, completion no longer reports `yin/def` or `:vm/store-put` for a\n   281\t   definition, where the old primitive profile did. The completion test now\n   282\t   asserts this. AST-side and segment-side requirements remain equal.\n   283\t6. **Construction refusal is by throwing.** The expander's `expand-batch`\n   284\t   throws on a ctx store that binds the name; it does not return error\n   285\t   data. I treat that as a composition defect, not a batch failure.\n   286\t7. **TDD order.** Most of the implementation came before its new tests,\n   287\t   which I wrote once the change surface was mapped. I did not do strict\n   288\t   red then green per feature. The new tests are load-bearing against the\n   289\t   base: the APIs they call and the refusals they assert do not exist at\n   290\t   96657a4f.\n   291\t8. **Walker hot loop.** `ast-walker-run-active-continuation` is private and\n   292\t   unused at base (kondo reports this before and after my change). I\n   293\t   updated it anyway so it stays consistent.\n   294\t9. **Findings the docs subagent reported** (not changed; for the owner):\n   295\t   - The UCF header still says \"Nothing below is implemented\". Its line-4\n   296\t     banner still says r3.\n   297\t   - `yin-repl-design.md` still says the ast-walker is the only backend.\n   298\t10. **One source edit after the final lanes.** I changed a docstring in\n   299\t    `code.cljc` (\"Rule 7\" to \"Rule 8\") after the final lanes finished. I\n   300\t    ran kondo and cljstyle on that file afterwards. The lanes did not rerun\n   301\t    after this docstring-only change.\n   302\t\n   303\t## Unrun checks\n   304\t\n   305\t- The parity harness ran only as part of the JVM, Node and Dart suites\n   306\t  (`parity_test`, `stack_parity_test`). I did not run a separate harness\n   307\t  command, and I did not find one in build-n-test.md.\n   308\t- New grid-table rows in semantic.md 2.4 and code-as-tuples 7.4, 7.5 and\n   309\t  7.7.1 are wider than 80 columns. A grid table needs every row at full\n   310\t  width. Every other added doc line passes the ASCII and 80-column check.\n   311\t- The docs subagent could not run git, so its own width check was partial.\n   312\t  I re-ran the ASCII and 80-column check over the full docs diff myself.\n   313\t- Commit two (the M2 linker records, the fetch contract requirement, and\n   314\t  deleting the round 3 and 4 guards) and the M4 bucket are out of scope and\n   315\t  were not touched.\n   316\t\n   317\tStatus: COMPLETE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
