{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\n     2\t  \"The store-write audit (Rule R, the store-key invariant): every program\n     3\t   store write goes through `yin.vm.engine/store-put`, which refuses a\n     4\t   reserved key; every other write into a store is state construction on\n     5\t   an exact allowlist. This gate greps the source tree for store writes\n     6\t   and fails on any site outside the allowlist, and on any allowlisted\n     7\t   site that no longer exists, so the list stays exact.\n     8\t\n     9\t   JVM only: it reads source files. The patterns are a heuristic over\n    10\t   one line each; a write the patterns cannot see is the residual this\n    11\t   gate documents rather than proves.\"\n    12\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    13\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    14\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(def ^:private store-write\n    18\t  \"One source line that writes into a store.\"\n    19\t  (re-pattern\n    20\t    (str/join \"|\"\n    21\t              [#\"\\(engine/store-put \"\n    22\t               #\"\\(store-put \\(:store \"\n    23\t               (str #\"\\((assoc|assoc-in|merge|dissoc|update|update-in) \"\n    24\t                    #\"(\\(:store [^)]*\\)|store)([ )]|$)\")\n    25\t               #\"\\(update(-in)? (\\S+ )?\\[?:store[ \\]]\"\n    26\t               #\"update :store \"\n    27\t               #\":store \\((assoc|merge|dissoc|into|conj|update)\\b\"\n    28\t               #\"\\(assoc \\S+ :store \\(:store \"])))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(def allowlist\n    32\t  \"file -> the exact trimmed lines, with the reason each may write.\"\n    33\t  {;; the one program write, and the dispatcher's :vm/store-put effect\n    34\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"\n    35\t   [\"(assoc store key val))\"\n    36\t    \":store (store-put (:store state)\"\n    37\t    ;; engine-minted keyword keys: stream ids, cursor ids, cursor advance\n    38\t    \"new-store (assoc (:store state) id handle)\"\n    39\t    \"new-store (assoc (:store state) id cursor-data)\"\n    40\t    \"(assoc store\"\n    41\t    \"(assoc store\"\n    42\t    ;; the ready-queue merge, asserted to carry only keyword keys\n    43\t    \":store (merge (:store state) updates)\"]\n    44\t   ;; program writes: the definition transition and the direct store\n    45\t   ;; instructions, through engine/store-put\n    46\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc\"\n    47\t   [\"state (assoc state :store (engine/store-put store (:name k) v))]\"\n    48\t    \"new-store (engine/store-put store key value)]\"\n    49\t    \"new-store (engine/store-put store key\"]\n    50\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc\"\n    51\t   [\"11 (let [vm' (assoc vm :store (engine/store-put (:store vm)\"\n    52\t    \"24 (let [vm' (assoc vm :store (engine/store-put (:store vm)\"]\n    53\t   ;; the constructor merge (checked) and the two program writes\n    54\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\"\n    55\t   [\":store (merge (:store base)\"\n    56\t    \":store (engine/store-put store key value)))\"\n    57\t    \":store (engine/store-put store (nth inst 1) value)))\"]\n    58\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc\"\n    59\t   [\":store (merge (:store base)\"\n    60\t    \":store (engine/store-put store key val)))\"\n    61\t    \":store (engine/store-put store (nth inst 2) val)))\"]\n    62\t   ;; dao.await: minted keyword keys, checked\n    63\t   \"src/cljc/dao/await.cljc\"\n    64\t   [\"(update :store merge store-updates))\"]\n    65\t   ;; the REPL's history keys: fixed symbols, none reserved\n    66\t   \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"\n    67\t   [\"(update state :vm update :store assoc\"]\n    68\t   ;; the handoff demo: shipped definitions, checked\n    69\t   \"src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc\"\n    70\t   [\"(update :store merge (vm/check-bindings! :store defs))\"]\n    71\t   ;; a JVM demo moving one VM's whole store to another\n    72\t   \"src/clj/yin/demo.clj\"\n    73\t   [\"other-vm' (assoc other-vm :store (:store current-vm))\"]\n    74\t   ;; the expander's macro store: harvest refuses the reserved key, and\n    75\t   ;; post-harvest installs only harvested names\n    76\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"\n    77\t   [\"(assoc store name (packet-of (index-of tree) value))\"\n    78\t    \"(dissoc store name)))\"\n    79\t    \"(assoc store nm (:macro-tree entry))\"\n    80\t    \"(dissoc store name)\"]})\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- source-files\n    84\t  []\n    85\t  (->> (file-seq (io/file \"src\"))\n    86\t       (filter #(.isFile ^java.io.File %))\n    87\t       (map #(.getPath ^java.io.File %))\n    88\t       (filter #(re-find #\"\\.clj[csd]?$\" %))\n    89\t       (remove #(str/includes? % \"/docs/\"))\n    90\t       sort))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn- store-writes\n    94\t  \"file -> the trimmed lines matching `store-write`, comments excluded.\"\n    95\t  []\n    96\t  (into {}\n    97\t        (keep (fn [f]\n    98\t                (let [hits (->> (str/split-lines (slurp f))\n    99\t                                (map #(first (str/split % #\";\" 2)))\n   100\t                                (filter #(re-find store-write %))\n   101\t                                (mapv str/trim))]\n   102\t                  (when (seq hits) [f hits]))))\n   103\t        (source-files)))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(deftest every-store-write-is-on-the-allowlist\n   107\t  (let [found (store-writes)]\n   108\t    (is (= (into {} (map (fn [[f ls]] [f (frequencies ls)])) allowlist)\n   109\t           (into {} (map (fn [[f ls]] [f (frequencies ls)])) found))\n   110\t        \"a new store write must go through engine/store-put or join the\n   111\t         allowlist with its reason\")))\n","exit_code":0,"sta