{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '805,860p;1354,1372p'\"","aggregated_output":"   805\t  discharge.\n   806\t- **Code:** every reachable segment's instructions are walked — as datoms\n   807\t  where the emitter holds the batch, as canonical tuples where only a vector\n   808\t  was fetched (§7.3.4) — including **`:store-get` and `:store-put`\n   809\t  operands**, which name store\n   810\t  keys directly and which the first draft missed entirely; every `:var`\n   811\t  name; every effect op (`:stream-*`, `:ffi-call`, and the effects of\n   812\t  `:effectful`-class primitives the walk finds); every `:resume` operand\n   813\t  (a parked id, §7.6.3). Discovering a new work item continues the fixed point\n   814\t  with that address and context even when the address was already walked for\n   815\t  another context.\n   816\t- **Names:** only a free `:var` name is an obligation. An obligation is\n   817\t  discharged by a matching key in the reachable store slice, or retained as\n   818\t  a required primitive or module export and checked by profile (§7.5.2). An\n   819\t  environment never discharges a name: captured environments contribute\n   820\t  values to their work item's reachability analysis, while lexical binding\n   821\t  determines whether a `:var` is free before it becomes an obligation. If no\n   822\t  store key or profiled primitive/module requirement can discharge an\n   823\t  obligation, discovery is `:incomplete`; after lowering, an unavailable\n   824\t  retained requirement is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` (§7.6.5).\n   825\t  Definitions are syntax (Rule R, S7.5.2): the definition operator\n   826\t  `yin/def` is never a free name and never an obligation, because a\n   827\t  well-formed segment has no `:var` naming it (`free-names` never returns\n   828\t  it); a `[:define name]` operand is a store key the segment writes, like\n   829\t  a `:store-put` operand, not a name it resolves.\n   830\t- **Modules:** a module's manifest declares its exported primitive profiles\n   831\t  and its **store footprint** (store keys and effect kinds its handlers may\n   832\t  touch). Until manifests carry footprints, any required module whose\n   833\t  footprint is undeclared sets `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` — the honest\n   834\t  statement that closure could not be computed, never a silent\n   835\t  under-approximation. A module effect handler may read store keys the\n   836\t  static walk cannot see; a composition may supply extra slice keys\n   837\t  explicitly, and the value records that it did.\n   838\t\n   839\tBecause the computation is over data, the same query answers \"what does this\n   840\tprogram need?\" for a segment that has never run. And because discovery can\n   841\t*fail to terminate successfully* — a missing segment cannot be walked, an\n   842\tundeclared footprint cannot be closed — the result distinguishes\n   843\t`:complete` from `:incomplete` from `:blocked` (§7.6.5); a fixed point that\n   844\tcould not finish is reported as such, not passed off as a satisfied closure.\n   845\t\n   846\t### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\n   847\t\n   848\tThe store S holds `def` results, stream handles, cursor entries, and the FFI\n   849\tpair (§4.1). None of it is global in the UCF sense; it is the emitter's. A\n   850\tcontinuation carries the **reachable slice**: every store key the fixed\n   851\tpoint of §7.6.1 can name — every free `:var` obligation for which the\n   852\temitter's store has a matching key, every `:store-get`/`:store-put` operand,\n   853\tevery stream/cursor cell — with values encoded by §7.5:\n   854\t\n   855\t```clojure\n   856\t:yin.k/store {counter 41\n   857\t              'log {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream …}}\n   858\t```\n   859\t\n   860\tThe FFI pair is never in the slice — a program that names the pair's store\n  1354\t  published revision history naming the complete execution contract\n  1355\t  (§7.3.3): the tuple grammar — mnemonic set, per-mnemonic arity and operand\n  1356\t  kinds, saturation/defaults table — the opcode table and transitions, the\n  1357\t  resolution and last-value-wins rules, the effect outcome map, and the\n  1358\t  scheduler semantics, written into `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4 beside the\n  1359\t  opcode table.\n  1360\t- **Primitive profile publication.** The standard `yin.vm/primitives`\n  1361\t  map published with profiles (S7.5.2), including the `:effectful`\n  1362\t  declaration for `require` (`yin/def` is syntax, not a primitive);\n  1363\t  reverse-lookup uniqueness asserted at `create-vm`.\n  1364\t- **Definition frames under Rule R.** The UCF frame encoding of a\n  1365\t  pending definition (a define continuation awaiting its value), stamp\n  1366\t  comparison at continuation lowering, module-store snapshot lowering\n  1367\t  through `engine/store-put`, and the lift and lower round trip of a\n  1368\t  parked definition are M4 obligations and do not pass today.\n  1369\t- **Discovery completeness.** The fixed point of §7.6.1 implemented and\n  1370\t  tested against the `:store-get`/`:store-put`, dynamic-callee, and\n  1371\t  cross-activation-`E` cases; module manifests publishing store footprints\n  1372\t  so `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` disappears.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
