{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '95,180p;475,525p' \"","aggregated_output":"    95\t  [opcode-table offset inst]\n    96\t  (reduce (fn [inst [i [_ kind]]]\n    97\t            (if (= :pc kind) (update inst (inc i) + offset) inst))\n    98\t          inst\n    99\t          (map-indexed vector (get opcode-table (nth inst 0)))))\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(defn- append-stack-image\n   103\t  \"Load `image` after the stack image `vm` already holds and start at its\n   104\t   first instruction.  A closure a previous input stored (a `def`) names a\n   105\t   body pc in the earlier image, so that image is kept, not replaced.\n   106\t   The incoming image is admitted alone by `load-image` under the current\n   107\t   stamp (the expander and the lowerer are its fresh producers), as\n   108\t   `append-register-image` admits its own; the image it runs in is the\n   109\t   concatenation. `:hash` stays the canonical H of the whole loaded\n   110\t   `:segment` (yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md), so each load hashes the\n   111\t   concatenation.\"\n   112\t  [vm image]\n   113\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   114\t        offset (count held)\n   115\t        shift #(relocate dcode/opcode-table offset %)\n   116\t        combined (into held (map shift) image)]\n   117\t    (assoc (stack/load-image vm image vm/stack-contract)\n   118\t           :segment combined\n   119\t           :hash (dcode/image-hash combined)\n   120\t           :pc offset)))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- append-register-image\n   124\t  \"The register image counterpart of `append-stack-image`.  The incoming\n   125\t   image is validated alone by `load-image`, which also sizes the register\n   126\t   file for its main body; the image it runs in is the concatenation, whose\n   127\t   later main bodies end in `:halt` as the first does.  `:hash` is the\n   128\t   canonical R of that concatenation (yin.vm.debruijn.register.md).\"\n   129\t  [vm {:keys [bodies instructions] :as image}]\n   130\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   131\t        offset (count (:instructions held))\n   132\t        shift-body #(-> % (update :start + offset) (update :end + offset))\n   133\t        shift #(relocate rcode/opcode-table offset %)\n   134\t        combined {:bodies (into (:bodies held) (map shift-body) bodies)\n   135\t                  :instructions (into (:instructions held)\n   136\t                                      (map shift)\n   137\t                                      instructions)}]\n   138\t    (assoc (register/load-image vm image vm/register-contract)\n   139\t           :segment combined\n   140\t           :hash (rcode/register-hash combined)\n   141\t           :pc offset)))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(def program-loaders\n   145\t  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\n   146\t   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\n   147\t   `[root rows]` (yin.vm.macro.md §2.4); each loader takes its row set — the\n   148\t   ast-walker through `vm-load-rows`, the semantic VM through\n   149\t   `linearize/rows-loader` over `semantic/load-vector`, and the de Bruijn\n   150\t   kernels through their lowerings to a stack image (H) or a register\n   151\t   image (R).  No evaluator learns that an expander ran.\"\n   152\t  {:ast-walker (fn [vm packet]\n   153\t                 (ast-walker/vm-load-rows vm\n   154\t                                          (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n   155\t                                          vm/ast-contract))\n   156\t   :semantic (let [load-rows (linearize/rows-loader semantic/load-vector)]\n   157\t               (fn [vm packet]\n   158\t                 (load-rows vm (macro/packet->row-set packet))))\n   159\t   :stack (fn [vm packet]\n   160\t            (append-stack-image\n   161\t              vm\n   162\t              (:image (debruijn-linearize/adapt\n   163\t                        (packet->named-datoms packet)))))\n   164\t   :register (fn [vm packet]\n   165\t               (append-register-image\n   166\t                 vm\n   167\t                 (:image (register-compile/adapt\n   168\t                           (packet->named-datoms packet)))))})\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(def lang-labels {:clojure \"Clojure\" :python \"Python\" :php \"PHP\"})\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(def command-heads\n   175\t  \"Commands this shell answers.  `connect` and `disconnect` belong to the\n   176\t   driver, which owns the RPC client; `telemetry` is answered only to say that\n   177\t   this REPL slice does not have it.\"\n   178\t  #{'vm 'lang 'compile 'reset 'help 'repl-state 'quit 'telemetry})\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   475\t(defn- standard-store\n   476\t  \"The expander store seeded with the standard forms, folded through the\n   477\t   same row-native batch contract as any input (yin.vm.macro.md §5.4).\"\n   478\t  []\n   479\t  (macro/seed-store (macro/make-ctx {:token :yin.repl/standard-forms\n   480\t                                     :source-medium :yin.repl/standard-forms})\n   481\t                    [macro/stdlib-forms]))\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t(defn- make-expander\n   485\t  \"The expander consumer for one session: a fresh incarnation token, the\n   486\t   `program-in` identity as its source medium, the standard store, and the\n   487\t   `program-out` writer.  No log writer: `(compile ...)` renders events.\"\n   488\t  [program-identity program-out]\n   489\t  (macro/make-expander\n   490\t    (macro/make-ctx {:token (str (random-uuid))\n   491\t                     :source-medium program-identity\n   492\t                     :store (standard-store)})\n   493\t    program-out))\n   494\t\n   495\t\n   496\t(defn- make-session\n   497\t  \"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\n   498\t   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\n   499\t   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\n   500\t   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\n   501\t   lifetime.\n   502\t\n   503\t   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   504\t   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   505\t   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   506\t   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   507\t   which loads each packet and runs it.\"\n   508\t  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   509\t  (let [vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives)\n   510\t        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n   511\t        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n   512\t    {:vm vm\n   513\t     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n   514\t     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n   515\t     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n   516\t     :observer (:observer program-in)\n   517\t     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n   518\t     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n   519\t     :row-observer (:observer program-out)}))\n   520\t\n   521\t\n   522\t(defn create-state\n   523\t  \"Create the shell value.  `:primitives` is a host-supplied map merged over\n   524\t   the REPL primitives; it is kept as `:extra-primitives` so every session\n   525\t   rebuild — `(reset)`, `(vm …)` — installs it again.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
