2. Re-pin the descriptor hash, every golden register vector, and\n   946\tevery R fixture because the descriptor hash is part of every R.\n   947\t\n   948\tR2 has no execution kernel dependency. Its completion criteria are:\n   949\t\n   950\t1. Every R2 node lowers to the exact tuple in section 4.6. Child evaluation\n  1102\t6. Allocation and any move order are canonicalized by evaluation and\n  1103\t   virtual-id order, with a versioned descriptor and golden fixtures.\n  1104\t7. The register kernel is a sibling and cannot silently replace the stack\n  1105\t   VM or alter its protocols.\n  1106\t8. B2 is the resolver-and-stack-lowerer split (section 2.2); the address\n  1107\t   law over the parity corpus remains a cross-check, not the coupling.\n  1108\t9. Live sets are in-band on every continuation boundary, as strictly\n  1109\t   ascending vectors computed by one exported backward-dataflow function,\n  1110\t   inside R's preimage, and recomputed by every receiver. R2 is register\n  1111\t   contract version 3. A saved continuation carries only live registers.\n  1112\t10. R2 defines effect opcodes, sparse continuation payloads, wait-entry\n  1113\t    shapes, and validation as pure data before R4 interprets them. The\n  1114\t    shared engine remains the sole owner of scheduling and wake disposition.\n  1115\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
